  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The intended audience is individuals who hold or are exposed to racially charged, economically reductive, and politically divisive narratives about South Africans, particularly those who support or sympathize with the stereotype that Black South Africans are passive recipients of exploitation and tolerant of theft by outsiders. The meme targets those who may identify with or propagate the 'racial hierarchy' and 'economic exploitation stereotype' tropes, and who are likely to engage with or share content that weaponizes racialized economic grievances. The reference to 'Cyril' (Cyril Ramaphosa) indicates the audience may include politically aware South Africans or international observers familiar with South African politics, who are being targeted with a hateful message that frames the South African government or people as complicit in or tolerant of economic injustice. The visual of the laughing man is used to project contempt and superiority, appealing to an audience that finds satisfaction in dehumanizing and stereotyping Black South Africans.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
